WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.900
What does Romans eight twenty-eight mean by good?

2
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.200
Paul says that all things

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.580
work together for good

4
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.020
for those who love God

5
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.000
and are called according to his purpose.

6
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.360
The next verse names that purpose:

7
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.320
being conformed to the image of his Son.

8
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.020
God is making his people like Christ.

9
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.760
The surrounding passage speaks honestly

10
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.400
about suffering, groaning, and waiting.

11
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.380
That gives this promise weight

12
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.560
when life is painful

13
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.100
and the future is unclear.

14
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.640
We may have to wait

15
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.720
without understanding how God is working.

16
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.840
But his purpose gives us reason to trust him.

17
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.200
When you return to this familiar promise,

18
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.200
read verse twenty-nine with it.

19
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.660
Let God's purpose shape your hope.
